    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Mason Estates are delighted to bring to the market this stylish two-bedroom apartment in the sought after gated development of St James`s Wood. This apartment is set in a small block which holds a nice position within the complex and comes with a secure parking space. It would suit a first time buyer or an investor looking for an ideal investment which is not rent capped. \n\nThe well-proportioned accommodation measuring circa 68sqm/732sqft is very presented in good condition and comprises of an entrance hallway with utility/hot-press plumbed for washing, large living/dining room with the kitchen off, two bedrooms and the bathroom. \n\nIdeally located on the tree lined South Circular Road close to the villages of Kilmainham and Rialto and with easy access to the City Centre. Just a short stroll from a host of local amenities including a choice of shops, post office, cafés, bars and restaurants, while recreational facilities such as the Irish Museum of Modern Art at Kilmainham Hospital, Phoenix Park and walks along the Grand Canal easily accessible. Nearby hospitals (within walking distance) include St James`s and the new National Children`s Hospital. There are excellent transport links with the Red LUAS line within minutes` walk, and the area is serviced by several regular public bus routes.\n\nTotal Floor Area: 68sq.m (743sq.ft.,) approx. \n\n(Note: images of some rooms online show current image and virtually staged image showing room décor potential).\n\nENTRANCE HALL: L-shaped 1.01m x 1.55m + 3.86m x 1.00m\nWelcoming hallway with ceiling rose and coving, laminate wood flooring, door to utility/hotpress (plumbed for washing machine). \n\nLIVING 5.43m x 5.18m / DINING ROOM: \nWonderfully spacious and bright room with laminate wood flooring, fireplace with timber surround, electric stove inset, room open to \n\nKITCHEN: 2.97m x 1.77m\nFully fitted kitchen with range of floor and wall mounted units, electric hob, oven, extractor fan, stainless steel sink, tiled splashback, laminate flooring. \n\nBEDROOM 1: 4.4m x 2.53m\nDouble bedroom with built-in wardrobes, laminate wood flooring.\n\nBEDROOM 2: 3.42m x 2.92m\nGenerously sized second double bedroom with built-in wardrobes, laminate wood flooring. \n \nBATHROOM: 2.18m x 1.83m\nFully tiled bathroom with bath, overhead shower, glass shower screen, wall mounted toiletries cabinet, shaving light, wash hand basin, w.c. \n\nOUTSIDE:\n\nCommunal and landscaped gardens. \n\nGENERAL POINTS: SERVICES: UTILITIES:\n\nBER: D1\nBER Number: 114171697 \nEnergy performance indicator: 254.04 kWh/m2/yr\nElectric Storage heating\nDouble glazed windows\n1x Car parking spaces (non-designated)\nBroadband available\nTV point\n\nManagement Company: Core Property Management\nService charge 2,010,69 (1,810.69 for early payment) \n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Notice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Spacious ground floor apartment with no rent cap </li><li> Outlook to wonderfully maintained internal courtyard </li><li> Small block within the development </li><li> Presented in good condition throughout </li><li> Secure parking space </li><li> Large choice of local amenities and recreational facilities </li><li> Several bus routes servicing the area and minutes` walk to Suir Road LUAS </li><li> Walking distance of St. James`s and the new National Children`s Hospital </li><li> Close to City Centre</li></ul>"
